XMLDocNormalizer - Checks and fixes C# XML documentation.&#xD;
Usage:&#xD;
  XMLDocNormalizer (--check | --fix) [--full] [--project projectName] [--test] [--clean-backups] [--verbose]&#xD;
                   [--format console|json|sarif] [--output path] [--exception-analysis-mode mode]&#xD;
                   [--compare-exception-analysis-modes]&#xD;
  --external-target &lt;job.json&gt;  Explicit local v1 unsigned single-project/root job (--check only); optional job analysisMode: direct|project-transitive|project-transitive-declared-exceptions (default). Paths relative to job file; no discovery or downloads.&#xD;
                   [--compare-value-documentation-modes]&#xD;
                   [--exception-analysis-comparison-runs n] [--exception-analysis-comparison-warmup-runs n] [path]&#xD;
                   [--value-documentation-mode mode]&#xD;
Options:&#xD;
  --check               Run in check-only mode (no changes).&#xD;
  --fix                 Run in fix mode (modifies files).&#xD;
  --full                Analyze all projects in a solution.&#xD;
  --project &lt;name&gt;      Analyze only the specified project in a solution.&#xD;
  --test                Use test mode (creates backups).&#xD;
  --clean-backups       Remove any backup files after run.&#xD;
  --verbose, -v         Enable verbose logging.&#xD;
  --format &lt;console|json|sarif&gt;  Output format.&#xD;
  --output &lt;path&gt;       File path for JSON/SARIF output.&#xD;
  --exception-analysis-mode &lt;mode&gt;&#xD;
                       Controls how exception documentation is analyzed.&#xD;
                       Values:&#xD;
                         direct&#xD;
                           Reports only directly thrown exceptions. Alias: d.&#xD;
                         project-transitive-declared-exceptions&#xD;
                           Reports all direct exceptions and follows calls within the reporting scope for exception types declared there.&#xD;
                           Aliases: ptd, declared, project-declared, project-transitive-declared.&#xD;
                         project-transitive&#xD;
                           Follows calls within the reporting scope. Aliases: pt, project.&#xD;
                         solution-transitive&#xD;
                           Follows calls across the loaded solution project-reference closure.&#xD;
                           Aliases: st, solution.&#xD;
                       Default: solution-transitive.&#xD;
  --value-documentation-mode &lt;mode&gt;&#xD;
                       Controls when missing &lt;value&gt; documentation is reported.&#xD;
                       Values: disabled, all-readable-properties, exclude-dto-like-types, indexers-only.&#xD;
                       Aliases: off, none, all, strict, readable-properties, exclude-dto-like, exclude-dto, non-dto, non-dto-like, indexer-only, indexers.&#xD;
                       Default: all-readable-properties.&#xD;
  --compare-exception-analysis-modes&#xD;
                       Executes all four exception analysis modes in isolated child processes and writes a comparison report.&#xD;
  --compare-value-documentation-modes&#xD;
                       Executes all value-documentation modes and writes a comparison report.&#xD;
  --exception-analysis-comparison-runs &lt;n&gt;&#xD;
                       Executes each exception analysis mode n measured times.&#xD;
                       Runs greater than 1 use rotating mode order and report median, mean, min, max and standard deviation.&#xD;
                       Default: 1.&#xD;
  --exception-analysis-comparison-warmup-runs &lt;n&gt;&#xD;
                       Executes each exception analysis mode n warmup times before measured runs.&#xD;
                       Warmup runs are excluded from timing statistics.&#xD;
                       Default: 0.&#xD;
  --enable-statistics           Generate statistics output for study/evaluation.&#xD;
  --statistics-output &lt;path&gt;    Write statistics JSON to the specified path.&#xD;
                       defaults to &lt;output&gt;_statistics.json when --output is set.&#xD;
  --include-generated   Includes generated files in analysis and metrics.&#xD;
  --include-tests       Includes test source files in analysis and metrics.&#xD;
  --help, -h            Show this help message.&#xD;
Examples:&#xD;
  XMLDocNormalizer --check --format console src/&#xD;
  XMLDocNormalizer --fix --test src/&#xD;
  XMLDocNormalizer --check --full MySolution.sln&#xD;
  XMLDocNormalizer --check --project MyProject MySolution.sln&#xD;
  XMLDocNormalizer --check --compare-exception-analysis-modes --exception-analysis-comparison-runs 5 MySolution.sln&#xD;
  XMLDocNormalizer --check --compare-exception-analysis-modes --exception-analysis-comparison-warmup-runs 1 --exception-analysis-comparison-runs 5 MySolution.sln&#xD;
  XMLDocNormalizer --check --value-documentation-mode exclude-dto-like-types MySolution.sln&#xD;
  XMLDocNormalizer --check --compare-value-documentation-modes --format json --output value-comparison.json MySolution.sln&#xD;
